[74/92] SuperGPQA/Sociology In 1814, 15 British individuals settled on T Island in the
The scenario describes a small founding population (15 British individuals) that settled on an isolated island, with one carrier of a recessive gene. Over time, the frequency of that gene became much higher than in the original population. This is a classic example of the **founder effect**, where a small group establishes a new population and carries only a subset of the genetic diversity from the original population, leading to a change in allele frequencies.

The other options (genetic drift, bottleneck, etc.) are related but less specific here. The founder effect is the most precise cause given the details.

