Third: \((x-18)(x-72) = x^2 -90x + 1296\).  
Sum = \(3x^2 - (170+116+90)x + (7056+1764+1296) = 3x^2 - 376x + 10116\).  
So  
\[
h(x) = \frac{3x^2 - 376x + 10116}{(x-18)(x-72)(x-98)}.
\]  
Thus equation becomes  
\[
\frac{3x^2 - 376x + 10116}{(x-18)(x-72)(x-98)} + \frac{1}{x-k} - \frac{1}{x} = 0.
\]  
Combine the last two:  
\[
\frac{1}{x-k} - \frac{1}{x} = \frac{x - (x-k)}{x(x-k)} = \frac{k}{x(x-k)}.
\]  
So equation:  
\[
\frac{3x^2 - 376x + 10116}{(x-18)(x-72)(x-98)} + \frac{k}{x(x-k)} = 0.
\]  
Thus  
\[
\frac{3x^2 - 376x + 10116}{(x-18)(x-72)(x-98)} = -\frac{k}{x(x-k)}.
\]  
Cross-multiply:  
\[
(3x^2 - 376x + 10116) \cdot x(x-k) = -k (x-18)(x-72)(x-98).
\]  
So  
\[
x(x-k)(3x^2 - 376x + 10116) + k (x-18)(x-72)(x-98) = 0.
