[76/92] COMPSEC/FreeBSD / librpcsec_gss rpcsec_gss_validate() reduction
The vulnerability is a stack buffer overflow. The `scratch` buffer is fixed at `AUTH_STACK_MAX` (256 bytes), but `encoded_len` can be up to `wire_left - 4`, which may exceed 256. The `memcpy` on line 20 copies `encoded_len` bytes into `scratch` without checking the size against the buffer's capacity.

The primary bug is introduced at line 20, where the unchecked copy occurs.

